01-02A read-only diagnosis — 2026-08-09

Runtime tuple before diagnosis: SILVER_MODE=legacy, GOLD_SOURCE=legacy, SHADOW_COMPARE=0

Iceberg REST container:
  service: de-demo-iceberg-rest
  CATALOG_URI: jdbc:sqlite:file:/catalog/iceberg_catalog.db
  CATALOG_CATALOG__IMPL: org.apache.iceberg.jdbc.JdbcCatalog
  mounted volume: de-practicum-demo_de_demo_iceberg_catalog
  catalog file: /catalog/iceberg_catalog.db (20480 bytes)

Independent catalog clients in the stack:
  iceberg-writer
  iceberg-medallion
  trino
  dbt-trino

Observed client-side failure from the failed canary:
  Medallion error: UncheckedSQLException: Unknown failure
  occurrences in filtered medallion log: 23

The REST log filter did not expose a literal SQLITE_BUSY line. This does not
clear SQLite: the configured JDBC backend is SQLite and the shared catalog is
being accessed by independent commit/query clients. No sleep, blind retry,
exception suppression, volume reset, table recreation, or data deletion was
performed.

PostgreSQL candidate is reachable (PostgreSQL 15.18), but a
metadata-preserving migration into it has not yet been proven. The rollout
therefore remains fail-closed at 01-02A and stays on legacy/legacy/0.
